Project: EduNexus

Root:
  ./

Architecture:
  ModularMonolith

Modules:
  # Business modules — see project/map.sdd for the full routing index.
  payment -> ./.sdd/project/payment
  course  -> ./.sdd/project/course
  user    -> ./.sdd/project/user

Domains:
  # Engineering disciplines, not business modules — see Skills below.
  Backend
  Frontend
  Mobile
  QA
  DevOps

Paths:
  BE: ./backend
  FE: ./frontend
  MD: ./mobile
  QA: ./qa
  DO: ./devops

ProjectModel:
  # WHAT / WHY / WHERE — "source of truth", never line-by-line code.
  root: ./.sdd/project
  map: ./.sdd/project/map.sdd
  modules: ./.sdd/project/modules.sdd
  dependencies: ./.sdd/project/dependencies.sdd
  architecture: ./.sdd/project/architecture.sdd
  integrations: ./.sdd/project/integrations.sdd
  proposals: ./.sdd/project/proposals
  per-module: ./.sdd/project/<module>/  (payment.sdd, flow.sdd, db.sdd, api.sdd, cases.sdd)

Flow:
  AN > AR > DB > BE > API > FE > MD > QA > DO > VR

  AN  = Analyze
  AR  = Architecture
  DB  = Database        (optional — see per-module flow.sdd condition)
  BE  = Backend
  API = API
  FE  = Frontend
  MD  = Mobile
  QA  = Quality Assurance
  DO  = DevOps
  VR  = Verify

  Full abbreviation table + optional-stage mechanism: ./.sdd/protocol/stages.sdd
  Per-feature execution chain lives in project/<module>/flow.sdd, not here
  (global files stay routing-only — see project/map.sdd).

Skills:
  BE: ./.sdd/backend
  FE: ./.sdd/frontend
  MD: ./.sdd/mobile
  QA: ./.sdd/qa
  DO: ./.sdd/devops

Chains:
  ./.sdd/chains

Prompts:
  root: ./.sdd/system/MASTER.md
  inbox: ./.sdd/prompts/inbox
  active: ./.sdd/prompts/active
  archive: ./.sdd/prompts/archive
  rejected: ./.sdd/prompts/rejected

Tasks:
  ./.sdd/tasks

Decisions:
  ./.sdd/decisions

StateSymbols:
  # Status vocabulary — see ./.sdd/protocol/symbols.sdd for the full spec.
  +  = DONE / PASS
  -  = FAIL
  ~  = IN_PROGRESS / ACTIVE
  !  = BLOCKED
  ?  = NEED_INPUT / DECISION
  >  = NEXT
  @  = REFERENCE
  #  = RULE

Rules:
  Human approval required before implementation.
  Failed task must return to the responsible stage (see protocol/rules.sdd).
  Failed review must not automatically skip to next stage.
  QA failure returns to implementation/review according to failure reason.
  DevOps failure returns to DevOps.
  Verification failure creates corrective task.
  Completed stages cannot be silently skipped.
  See protocol/rules.sdd -> RULE: CHAIN_INTEGRITY for the full enforcement contract.

AdaptivePipeline:
  Default Flow above is not mandatory for every task.
  Each task/feature declares its own "Required stages" subset in its chain file.

  Example — backend-only bugfix:
    BE -> QA -> VR

  Example — UI-only change:
    FE -> MD -> QA -> VR

  Example — infrastructure-only change:
    DO -> VR

Note:
  This is a template/example instance derived from the EduNexus illustration
  used in the source conversation (prompt/new/1.md..10.md). When applied to
  a real project, this file and ./project/* MUST be regenerated from
  evidence per project/architecture.sdd -> ProjectInstantiation, not copied
  as-is. PROJECT.sdd itself never holds project knowledge — it only routes
  to where that knowledge lives (see ProjectModel above).
